{
  "name": "Enrich spreadsheet rows with work email, job title and profile URL",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Enrich spreadsheet rows with work email, job title and profile URL\n\n### How it works\nFill the gaps in a list you already own. The sheet holds full_name and domain per row; email, title, seniority, profile and status start empty. Each run reads the rows without a status, takes at most max_rows of them and asks Argorant to find each person at their company. A match with a passing email writes the email, title, seniority and profile URL back to the row; a miss writes not found, so the row is not tried again.\n\nCosts: 1 credit per person found with a passing email; misses are free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns full_name, domain, email, title, seniority, profile, status and pick it in both Google Sheets nodes.\n4. Set max_rows in **Settings** and click Execute workflow.\n\n### Customization\nAdd a schedule trigger to enrich new rows every hour.",
        "height": 558,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "60f4e35a-7f6e-47e2-9de8-3b1cc27eaef2",
